# Executive verdict

**Recommendation: retain the publication project and revise the existing paper, rather than restart it. The core mathematics is considerably stronger than the standalone evidence package.**

The manuscript has a viable center: an exact $n$-query lower bound for recovery of an $n$-bit Bernstein--Vazirani secret in the stated characteristic-two linear-modal model, including arbitrary finite ancillas and finite adaptive complete instruments. Standard XOR access attains that bound. I reconstructed the argument, examined its treatment of classical histories and vanishing branches, and obtained an alternative proof using the degree of a single secret-indicator polynomial. I did not identify a fatal error in any of the seven numbered mathematical results.

This is not an unconditional approval of the archive for submission. The original experimental supplement, canonical runner, historical datasets, and several referenced provenance records are absent. The manuscript also retains an author-placeholder footnote and internal publication-workflow prose. Its theorem-level priority remains unresolved: several ingredients are definitely prior art, while a source with the full claimed adaptive BV or generalized DJ statement was not located in the primary-source passages inspected. That negative search result does not certify novelty.

**Weighted readiness: 7.388/10, reported as 7.4/10.** This is an editorial assessment of the submitted archive, not a probability of acceptance, not a proof certificate, and not a score for a hypothetical repaired paper.

The strongest result is Theorem 4.2, supported by Lemma 4.1. The Deutsch and Deutsch--Jozsa arguments are sound and compact. The ring proposition is also correct, but is secondary to the paper's query-complexity contribution. The weakest parts are the unsupported portability of historical experimental claims and the unresolved distinction between a useful new quantified theorem and a straightforward specialization of known methods.

The best present form is a **focused technical note**. Put exact BV recovery and the adaptive recording argument at its center; retain Deutsch/DJ as clean related obstructions; keep UNIQUE-SAT as a short, explicitly attributed positive control. The ring example can be a compact appendix. The small Simon experiment belongs in the reproducibility supplement unless it carries a specific explanatory burden.

