| Feature | Field lower bounds | Matching upper bounds | Ring example |
|:--|:--|:--|:--|
| Scalars | Any characteristic-two field | Same field, Boolean basis labels | $A=\mathbb F_2[u]/(u^4)$ |
| States/spaces | Nonzero vectors; finite dimension per node | Basis-state constructions suffice | Free modules; specify primitive vectors where used |
| Composition | Tensor over $F$ | Tensor over $F$ | Tensor over $A$ |
| Gates | Secret-independent invertible maps/injections | Fixed Boolean basis permutations and allowed readout | Invertible $A$-linear maps |
| Ancillas | Arbitrary finite | Finite work/answer storage | No universal ancilla lower bound asserted |
| Measurement | Finite stack-injective linear instruments | Complete basis readout | Nonzero contractions in worked example |
| Adaptivity | Finite recorded tree | Not needed for displayed optima | No general adaptive query theorem |
| Oracle | Fixed pointwise invertible actions; node-specific pairs allowed | Standard QXOR specifically | Flip or separately declared cyclic action |
| Inverses | Lower-bound argument persists | QXOR is its own inverse | Construction-specific |
| Exactness | Every possible output correct; no vanished total record | Same requirement | Analyzer claim is algebraic |
| Exclusions | Postselection, nonlinear updates, free coefficient table, unbounded stopping | Same exclusions | No silent scalar/tensor reinterpretation |

A complete instrument is not a choice to keep only a successful outcome. Its stack has trivial kernel. This is decisive: allowing arbitrary postselection could invalidate the nonzero-record step. Arbitrary finite workspace is permitted, but no uniform gate-efficiency theorem is claimed. An exponential-size secret-independent measurement may be allowed by a pure query model; it would require separate treatment in a computational-complexity model.

The equal-action case $G_0=G_1$ is a legitimate member of the lower-bound class, not evidence that QXOR has infinite complexity. Similarly, an inverse action remains affine in the Boolean control, but an entirely different phase/cyclic access primitive must not inherit the QXOR cost label without an implementation argument.

